function Markdown({ children }: { children: string })
One markdown renderer for READMEs and docs. react-markdown never renders
raw HTML, so third-party README content stays inert by default.

function StorageWarning()
Shown whenever the server is holding posts in memory. Saving is refused in
 that state, so this explains the refusal before it happens.

const PreviewLayout = React.lazy(() => import("@/pages/preview/PreviewLayout"))
The preview pulls in react-markdown and the 71-document manifest, and mermaid
on top of that — none of which the landing page should pay for.

function BackToTop()
Appears once the page is a couple of screens deep, and gets out of the way
 again on the way back up.

function GithubMark(props: SVGProps<SVGSVGElement>)
lucide-react v1 dropped brand marks, so the GitHub glyph is inlined here.
Sized and stroked to sit next to lucide icons without looking foreign.

